#
#   host - The QuickJS C library: what a runner and a simple embedder need around the engine
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of the parts of quickjs-libc.c (QuickJS 2026-06-04) that run JavaScript files
#       and QuickJS's own tests: the global helpers (print, console.log, scriptArgs), the
#       default module loader reading files, the job and timer loop, and the `std` and `os`
#       modules on POSIX targets (macOS and Linux), with their processes, pipes, signals,
#       read/write handlers and ttys, and the running of precompiled bytecode. Workers and
#       their message ports and shared-library modules are not ported. This fragment holds
#       the module's imports and the per-runtime state (JSThreadState); the C library
#       bindings are in `libc` and `libc_process`.
